<title>USA: Maryland switches Medicaid participants to HMOs.</title>
<headline>Maryland switches Medicaid participants to HMOs.</headline>
<dateline>ANNAPOLIS, Md. 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>A new Maryland law taking effect Monday will require more than 350,000 state Medicaid recipients to switch to Health Maintenance Organizations for their health care.</p>
<p>The revised Medicaid program, which pays for health care for low-income people, now limits participants choices to specific lists of managed care medical groups.</p>
<p>State officials estimate the program will save Maryland almost $50 million in health care costs.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
